  "problem": "Find the contrapositive of the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ **If** you need an umbrella, **then** the sky is not clear.",
  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ You need an umbrella.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ The sky is not clear.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A\u21d2B$ is given by \n\n$$\n\u00acB\u21d2\u00acA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $\u00acA:$ You do not need an umbrella.\n\n- $\u00acB:$ The sky is clear.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If the sky is clear, then you do not need an umbrella.",
